{
  "an2.52:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 2.52–63 ",
  "an2.52:0.2": "The Chapter on Individuals ",
  "an2.52:1.0": "52 ",
  "an2.52:1.1": "“These two individuals, mendicants, arise in the world for the welfare and happiness of the people, for the people, for the benefit, welfare, and happiness of gods and humans. ",
  "an2.52:1.2": "What two? ",
  "an2.52:1.3": "The Realized One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha; and the wheel-turning monarch. ",
  "an2.52:1.4": "These are the two individuals who arise in the world for the welfare and happiness of the people, for the people, for the benefit, welfare, and happiness of gods and humans.” ",
  "an2.53:1.0": "53 ",
  "an2.53:1.1": "“These two individuals, mendicants, arise in the world who are incredible human beings. ",
  "an2.53:1.2": "What two? ",
  "an2.53:1.3": "The Realized One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha; and the wheel-turning monarch. ",
  "an2.53:1.4": "These are the two individuals who arise in the world who are incredible human beings.” ",
  "an2.54:1.0": "54 ",
  "an2.54:1.1": "“There are two individuals, mendicants, whose death is regretted by many people. ",
  "an2.54:1.2": "What two? ",
  "an2.54:1.3": "The Realized One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha; and the wheel-turning monarch. ",
  "an2.54:1.4": "These are the two individuals, mendicants, whose death is regretted by many people.” ",
  "an2.55:1.0": "55 ",
  "an2.55:1.1": "“Mendicants, these two are worthy of a monument. ",
  "an2.55:1.2":